Subject: Cantor Supervised Local Lifecycle Operational Faults

@ [authority] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Supervised_Local_Lifecycle.sop
@ [proof] C:\Project\Cantor\proofs\Cantor_Supervised_Local_Lifecycle_Proof.sop

& [FaultRecordIdentity] is the resolved lifecycle ledger
  + [record_uuid] is bbb491cc-8932-4656-b1b0-6e43f4bec647
  + [captured_at_ms] is 1785385157430
  + [status] is resolved_with_no_open_product_fault

& [ExecutionPolicyBoundary] is expected operator behavior
  + [observation] is this machine blocks direct unsigned module import under its default Windows PowerShell execution policy
  + [resolution] is every documented and tested operator entry uses powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File
  + [security_note] is this selects local script execution but does not expand Cantor service, semantic, or token authority
  + [status] is documented

& [ExtendedPathHarnessFault] is caught by the first integration run
  + [observation] is Rust canonicalization produced a Windows \\?\ script path for which Windows PowerShell left PSScriptRoot null
  + [repair] is normalize only the subprocess-test path representation to ordinary absolute Windows form
  + [product_boundary] is production scripts continue to require ordinary absolute operator paths and reject ambiguous artifacts
  + [status] is resolved

& [DetachedPipeHarnessHang] is caught by the second integration run
  + [observation] is Command.output pipe capture around a launcher can remain open through the detached service child and block the test harness
  + [repair] is start supervision uses null standard handles in the test harness while state is the durable readiness artifact and health plus stop retain captured machine JSON
  + [cleanup] is the exact orphaned test process was stopped and its exact cantord child was shut down through authenticated generation-bound stop
  + [status] is resolved

& [PIDReuseRisk] is resolved in design and proof
  + [observation] is a PID file can target an unrelated later process
  + [repair] is require PID, canonical executable, and exact process start time together for health, stale-state replacement, failed-start cleanup, and shutdown
  + [proof] is a live PID with forged start time could neither report health nor stop the real service
  + [status] is resolved

& [ReadinessFaultOpacity] is resolved during review
  + [observation] is the first bounded readiness loop discarded the last probe reason
  + [repair] is retain and report the last bounded secret-free probe fault while preserving cleanup
  + [status] is resolved

& [ConcurrentStartRace] is resolved during post-checkpoint review
  + [observation] is two launchers could both pass an absent-state check before either published readiness
  + [risk] is a losing bind attempt could transiently probe the winner and confuse process ownership
  + [repair] is hold a state-path-derived local kernel mutex across collision review, launch, readiness, state publication, and failed-start cleanup
  + [proof] is two simultaneous real-binary start attempts produced exactly one success, one healthy state owner, and one graceful stop
  + [status] is resolved

& [ReadinessDeadlineDrift] is resolved during post-checkpoint review
  + [observation] is the initial outer readiness deadline did not cap one client process or the final retry sleep
  + [risk] is a short supervisor deadline could be exceeded by the service-configured client timeout
  + [repair] is cap every client process and sleep interval to the exact remaining outer deadline
  + [status] is resolved

& [DuplicateStateMemberAcceptance] is resolved during post-checkpoint review
  + [observation] is Windows PowerShell ConvertFrom-Json silently retains the last of two identically named properties
  + [risk] is an ambiguous state record could pass property-set validation
  + [repair] is require strict UTF-8 without BOM and exact compact decode-encode byte equality before any field or process authority is used
  + [proof] is a duplicate schema member is rejected while the original canonical state remains healthy
  + [status] is resolved

& [EvidenceLineEndingPortability] is resolved during repository audit
  + [observation] is core.autocrlf was true while raw-byte evidence manifests hashed text artifacts and PowerShell JSON contained mixed CRLF and LF
  + [risk] is a clean Windows checkout could change evidence bytes and invalidate a manifest described as clone-portable
  + [repair] is enforce LF for every hashed non-SOP text type, preserve SOP bytes as non-text authority, emit LF-only generated JSON, and bind .gitattributes into every current evidence manifest
  + [status] is resolved
